Run cat > /tmp/kspec-review-01KJXSVJK7DS2RV2SNMYH5G39W.json <<'EOF'
[
  {
    "command": "task note",
    "args": {
      "ref": "@01KJXSVJK7DS2RV2SNMYH5G39W",
      "message": "Review findings: MUST-FIX 1) packages/web-ui/src/routes/plans/+page.svelte:285 and :297 add plan-scoped \"View Specs\" / \"View Tasks\" links, but the destination pages ignore the plan query. /items only redirects to /specs preserving query (packages/web-ui/src/routes/items/+page.svelte:8-10), /specs only reads ref (packages/web-ui/src/routes/specs/+page.svelte:53-58), and /tasks only supports status/type/tag/assignee/automation filters (packages/web-ui/src/routes/tasks/+page.svelte:39-46; packages/web-ui/src/lib/api.ts:95-103). Clicking the new actions therefore lands on unfiltered lists, so the wireframe navigation action is still not implemented. SHOULD-FIX 2) packages/web-ui/tests/e2e/plans.spec.ts:185-202 only asserts that the buttons are visible; it never verifies the href or filtered navigation behavior, which let this regression through. Tests passed (npm test; cd packages/web-ui && npm test), and kspec validate showed no warnings for @ui-plans-view."
    }
  },
  {
    "command": "task needs-work",
    "args": {
      "ref": "@01KJXSVJK7DS2RV2SNMYH5G39W",
      "reason": "Review issues: plan action links on /plans navigate with ?plan=..., but /specs and /tasks ignore that parameter, so View Specs / View Tasks do not show the selected plan's linked records."
    }
  }
]
EOF
kspec batch --file /tmp/kspec-review-01KJXSVJK7DS2RV2SNMYH5G39W.json

